WEBVTT

00:00:00.371 --> 00:00:02.332
African Safari won.

00:00:02.392 --> 00:00:04.614
Breakfast time.

00:00:04.674 --> 00:00:08.245
It is very early in the morning.

00:00:08.305 --> 00:00:13.978
Adam and Lily are going on Safari in Kenya.

00:00:14.038 --> 00:00:19.250
Their friend Joseph is waiting for them.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:24.912
Look Adam, I can see him.

00:00:24.972 --> 00:00:32.866
The airplane is arriving at a small airport in the Masai Mara.

00:00:32.926 --> 00:00:37.079
Joseph is standing near his jeep.

00:00:37.139 --> 00:00:40.712
He works in the game reserve.

00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:50.140
Today he is meeting Adam, Lily and some American visitors.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:57.873
The friends say hello and get into the jeep.

00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:02.194
This is Anne.

00:01:02.253 --> 00:01:07.006
Behind her are Jeff and his son Tom.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.528
Hi.

00:01:08.588 --> 00:01:11.420
Is this your first safari?

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.480
Yes.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.972
I can't wait.

00:01:15.032 --> 00:01:19.404
I know that face.

00:01:19.464 --> 00:01:23.177
Tom wants to see the big five.

00:01:23.237 --> 00:01:24.258
Yes.

00:01:24.318 --> 00:01:25.358
Look.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:28.180
I've got a book about them.

00:01:28.239 --> 00:01:32.090
That woman is very quiet.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:35.422
Who is she?

00:01:35.482 --> 00:01:38.404
Hey, listen.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.244
Can you hear that?

00:01:40.304 --> 00:01:41.585
A lion?

00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:42.566
Quick!

00:01:42.626 --> 00:01:44.616
Let's go!

00:01:44.676 --> 00:01:54.277
Joseph drives the jeep across the country.

00:01:54.337 --> 00:01:59.896
Look!

00:01:59.956 --> 00:02:02.408
Zebra for breakfast!

00:02:02.468 --> 00:02:04.148
Quiet, Jeff.

00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:09.872
You don't see this very often.

00:02:09.932 --> 00:02:14.056
Zoe.

00:02:14.116 --> 00:02:15.537
Lily's friend.

00:02:15.597 --> 00:02:19.510
Is at home in London.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.382
Look, Dan.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:25.404
This is from Lily.

00:02:25.464 --> 00:02:28.198
Is she in Africa now?

00:02:28.258 --> 00:02:30.640
Yes, she is.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.432
Listen.

00:02:32.492 --> 00:02:34.594
Hi Zoe.

00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:38.706
We arrived in Kenya yesterday.

00:02:38.766 --> 00:02:42.409
Now we're on safari.

00:02:42.469 --> 00:02:45.502
In the Masai Mara.

00:02:45.562 --> 00:02:48.284
Joseph is with us.

00:02:48.344 --> 00:02:52.606
He was Adam's student in Nairobi.

00:02:52.666 --> 00:02:55.642
He's a driver now.

00:02:55.701 --> 00:03:01.166
There are three Americans in our Jeep.

00:03:01.226 --> 00:03:04.567
I'm sending you some photos.

00:03:04.627 --> 00:03:09.778
The woman doesn't smile or talk to us.

00:03:09.838 --> 00:03:13.089
We were lucky this morning.

00:03:13.149 --> 00:03:20.301
A lion had a zebra for breakfast in front of our Jeep.

00:03:20.361 --> 00:03:25.085
I've got about 100 photos of it.

00:03:25.144 --> 00:03:30.742
It's okay, there was no danger.

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:35.716
Tomorrow we're going to get up at five.

00:03:35.776 --> 00:03:40.209
We want to see some elephants.

00:03:40.268 --> 00:03:49.817
Dan, I know that woman in the hat, but I can't remember her name.

00:03:49.876 --> 00:03:52.028
Do you know?

00:03:52.088 --> 00:03:57.206
Let's see the photos.

00:03:57.266 --> 00:04:02.172
The big five.

00:04:02.232 --> 00:04:05.503
Joseph loves his job.

00:04:05.563 --> 00:04:10.575
The day starts very early at five o'clock.

00:04:10.635 --> 00:04:17.018
Every day he drives visitors across the Masai Mara.

00:04:17.078 --> 00:04:20.891
Often breakfast is in the jeep.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:26.654
They stop near the river Mara and watch the hippos.

00:04:26.714 --> 00:04:30.895
They see the giraffes in the trees.

00:04:30.955 --> 00:04:36.357
Families of zebras are eating grass.

00:04:36.417 --> 00:04:43.336
Then, Joseph and his visitors look for the big five.

00:04:43.396 --> 00:04:49.460
The big five are big, strong animals.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:05:00.371
They are lions, leopards, elephants, buffaloes and rhinoceroses.

00:05:00.431 --> 00:05:04.680
They are all very dangerous.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:14.117
Lions and leopards usually hunt for food at night and sleep in the day.

00:05:14.176 --> 00:05:19.608
Lions hunt and kill big animals.

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:27.939
They eat giraffes, zebras and other big five animals.

00:05:27.999 --> 00:05:35.650
Leopards eat meat too, but they like to eat small animals.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:38.833
First, they kill them.

00:05:38.892 --> 00:05:44.866
Then, they often take the dead animals up into the trees.

00:05:44.926 --> 00:05:48.538
There, they eat them slowly.

00:05:48.598 --> 00:05:52.570
Buffalo's live in big groups.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:57.753
They are very strong, and they can kill a lion.

00:05:57.813 --> 00:06:05.006
They eat green food, tall grass and other plants.

00:06:05.066 --> 00:06:10.798
They like the rain and they like to be near water.

00:06:10.858 --> 00:06:15.290
They live for about 17 years.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:19.452
Rhinos are endangered animals.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:26.876
There are only about 40 black rhinos in the Masai Mara today.

00:06:26.936 --> 00:06:32.128
Some people hunt rhinos because of their horns.

00:06:32.188 --> 00:06:38.802
In some countries, people give a lot of money for a rhino horn.

00:06:38.862 --> 00:06:41.694
This is a big problem.

00:06:41.754 --> 00:06:48.318
The police and the keepers want to stop them, but that is difficult.

00:06:48.378 --> 00:06:53.630
Rhinos eat grass and fruit, but no meat.

00:06:53.689 --> 00:06:55.968
They sleep in the day.

00:06:56.028 --> 00:06:59.972
Sometimes they sleep on their feet.

00:07:00.032 --> 00:07:04.515
Elephants live in big family groups.

00:07:04.575 --> 00:07:06.876
They don't eat meat.

00:07:06.936 --> 00:07:12.381
They only eat trees, plants and fruit.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:19.420
They are very intelligent and they can understand other elephants.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:26.618
They make noises, but people can't always hear them.

00:07:26.678 --> 00:07:36.236
African Safari 2, a long afternoon.

00:07:36.296 --> 00:07:42.920
The Jeep stops near a river.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.622
Look!

00:07:44.682 --> 00:07:46.754
Hippos!

00:07:46.814 --> 00:07:48.757
Wait!

00:07:48.817 --> 00:07:50.780
I'm coming.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:57.012
Lily, that woman's name is Ruth Street.

00:07:57.072 --> 00:08:01.744
She's American, but she lives in London.

00:08:01.804 --> 00:08:06.165
Her photo was in the newspapers yesterday.

00:08:06.225 --> 00:08:09.756
The police are looking for her.

00:08:09.816 --> 00:08:17.060
She buys rhino horns for a group.

00:08:17.119 --> 00:08:22.862
Look at that mouth!

00:08:22.922 --> 00:08:26.113
He wants to eat your bag, Lily.

00:08:26.173 --> 00:08:28.173
No, he doesn't.

00:08:28.233 --> 00:08:29.294
Look!

00:08:29.354 --> 00:08:31.404
Buffalo's!

00:08:31.464 --> 00:08:35.214
But where are the elephants?

00:08:35.274 --> 00:08:40.555
We're going to find them now, Tom.

00:08:40.616 --> 00:08:43.836
Let's go.

00:08:43.896 --> 00:08:45.887
It's going to rain.

00:08:45.946 --> 00:08:47.857
Yes, please.

00:08:47.917 --> 00:08:49.712
Let's go.

00:08:49.772 --> 00:08:55.850
Suddenly it was dark and the rain started.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.603
I'm going to stop.

00:08:58.662 --> 00:09:00.113
I can't see.

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:05.037
I don't like this.

00:09:05.097 --> 00:09:08.810
Is that an elephant?

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:09.960
Yes.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.142
The mother's behind him.

00:09:13.202 --> 00:09:17.306
Lily wants to adopt an elephant.

00:09:17.366 --> 00:09:18.962
Lily?

00:09:19.022 --> 00:09:20.578
Excuse me.

00:09:20.638 --> 00:09:23.020
Oh, yes.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.073
I want to visit the elephant orphanage.

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:29.184
Good.

00:09:29.244 --> 00:09:32.186
Ah, the rain's stopping.

00:09:32.246 --> 00:09:33.267
Let's go.

00:09:33.287 --> 00:09:40.972
Look at this, Adam.

00:09:41.032 --> 00:09:43.023
Oh, Lily.

00:09:43.083 --> 00:09:46.778
Is it from Zoe?

00:09:46.839 --> 00:09:51.134
adopt an elephant.

00:09:51.195 --> 00:09:54.126
This is Shukuru.

00:09:54.186 --> 00:09:56.718
She is from Sarvo.

00:09:56.778 --> 00:10:03.872
Today she lives in the Sheldrik elephant orphanage near Nairobi.

00:10:03.932 --> 00:10:08.514
She arrived at the orphanage in September 2009.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:12.046
She was only three days old.

00:10:12.106 --> 00:10:19.262
Now she has a new family and a lot of friends.

00:10:19.322 --> 00:10:21.753
Visitors can meet her.

00:10:21.813 --> 00:10:29.078
They can adopt her too, but she is always going to live in Africa.

00:10:29.138 --> 00:10:32.900
A lot of people visit the orphanage.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:40.074
At 11 o'clock in the morning, the elephants come out with their keepers.

00:10:40.134 --> 00:10:43.594
The elephants run and play.

00:10:43.654 --> 00:10:47.833
Then the keepers give them their food.

00:10:47.893 --> 00:10:53.674
Sometimes a young rhino comes out and plays too.

00:10:53.734 --> 00:11:01.516
The visitors stand very near the animals and take a lot of photos.

00:11:01.576 --> 00:11:08.238
The animals are in the orphanage because they haven't got families.

00:11:08.298 --> 00:11:11.918
The keepers are their mothers.

00:11:11.978 --> 00:11:21.903
After some time, perhaps ten years, the elephants go back into the wild.

00:11:21.963 --> 00:11:30.128
Samson's Story The year was 1954.

00:11:30.188 --> 00:11:35.252
There was very little rain in the Sarvo Game Reserve.

00:11:35.312 --> 00:11:40.284
Some visitors arrived and they loved Savo.

00:11:40.344 --> 00:11:45.105
One evening they watched a family of elephants.

00:11:45.165 --> 00:11:50.606
One young elephant was very thin and unhappy.

00:11:50.666 --> 00:11:54.527
He was ill and he wanted water.

00:11:54.587 --> 00:11:58.668
He walked slowly behind his mother.

00:11:58.728 --> 00:12:04.498
The elephants arrived at the water and started to drink.

00:12:04.558 --> 00:12:09.540
The young elephant wanted to stay near the water.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:12.782
His mother wanted to go.

00:12:12.842 --> 00:12:21.298
She didn't want to go away from her son, but she went with the other elephants.

00:12:21.358 --> 00:12:25.500
The visitors watched the young elephant.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:27.432
He was lucky.

00:12:27.492 --> 00:12:32.358
No lions or other animals came near him.

00:12:32.418 --> 00:12:39.798
The elephant was the first orphan in David Sheldrick's elephant orphanage.

00:12:39.858 --> 00:12:44.632
His name was Samson.

00:12:44.692 --> 00:12:49.196
African Safari 3.

00:12:49.256 --> 00:12:52.008
Where is Anne?

00:12:52.068 --> 00:12:56.112
I don't like that girl.

00:12:56.172 --> 00:13:00.088
She's always looking at me.

00:13:00.148 --> 00:13:04.634
The police are looking for you.

00:13:04.694 --> 00:13:08.567
Go away for a week or two.

00:13:08.627 --> 00:13:14.561
Go on safari or to the desert.

00:13:14.621 --> 00:13:17.973
Where's Anne this morning?

00:13:18.033 --> 00:13:20.764
She wasn't at breakfast.

00:13:20.824 --> 00:13:22.996
We can't wait.

00:13:23.056 --> 00:13:26.648
We're going to see the rhinos this morning.

00:13:26.709 --> 00:13:27.759
Okay?

00:13:27.819 --> 00:13:35.775
Let's go.

00:13:35.835 --> 00:13:44.880
Can we get out?

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:46.391
Yes.

00:13:46.451 --> 00:13:49.422
The keepers are always near them.

00:13:49.482 --> 00:13:55.494
Lily looks at the rhinos and thinks about Anne.

00:13:55.554 --> 00:13:58.805
Smile, Tom.

00:13:58.865 --> 00:14:02.456
Jeff is smiling too.

00:14:02.516 --> 00:14:07.478
He's got photos of four of the big five.

00:14:07.538 --> 00:14:09.408
Thanks, Joseph.

00:14:09.468 --> 00:14:12.080
That was a beautiful day.

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:14.503
Lipids tomorrow, Tom.

00:14:14.563 --> 00:14:17.804
And Masai dancing this evening.

00:14:17.864 --> 00:14:23.716
Adam, let's find Anne.

00:14:23.776 --> 00:14:27.848
She isn't here.

00:14:27.908 --> 00:14:30.469
And her things aren't here.

00:14:30.529 --> 00:14:35.831
Where is she?

00:14:35.891 --> 00:14:41.212
The Masai people.

00:14:41.272 --> 00:14:45.782
The Masai are very interesting people.

00:14:45.842 --> 00:14:52.626
Many live in Kenya, near the Masai Mara game reserve.

00:14:52.686 --> 00:14:58.259
The men and the women are tall and strong.

00:14:58.319 --> 00:15:05.834
Every day they walk across the country with their cows and their goats.

00:15:05.894 --> 00:15:13.479
There is very little grass in the Masai Mara and very little rain.

00:15:13.539 --> 00:15:20.492
The men and boys hunt wild animals and bring them back home.

00:15:20.552 --> 00:15:25.565
Sometimes very young boys kill lions.

00:15:25.626 --> 00:15:31.560
This is dangerous, but for the Masai it is important.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:37.544
The Masai dress in beautiful colours, usually red.

00:15:37.604 --> 00:15:40.817
They like dancing and singing.

00:15:40.877 --> 00:15:49.134
Sometimes they sing and dance for visitors at the hotels in the game reserve.

00:15:49.194 --> 00:15:55.152
Masai women don't hunt, but they do a lot of work.

00:15:55.212 --> 00:15:59.096
They build the houses for their families.

00:15:59.156 --> 00:16:09.099
The Masai people move from place to place, and the women build new homes in the new places.

00:16:09.159 --> 00:16:16.570
Every morning they get up very early and bring water for their families.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:25.218
This is a very important job because water is a big problem for the Masai.

00:16:25.278 --> 00:16:28.192
The women make the food too.

00:16:28.252 --> 00:16:34.019
The Masai eat meat and they eat food from plants.

00:16:34.079 --> 00:16:38.272
Not all Masai children go to school.

00:16:38.332 --> 00:16:42.686
Often there are no schools near their homes.

00:16:42.746 --> 00:16:50.054
School is expensive too and many families haven't got the money.

00:16:50.114 --> 00:16:56.518
Today, many Maasai people live and work in towns.

00:16:56.578 --> 00:17:02.821
Sometimes they visit their families and friends.

00:17:02.881 --> 00:17:11.296
African Safari 4, a good day for rhinos.

00:17:11.355 --> 00:17:16.339
Your taxi is coming now, Miss Wilson.

00:17:16.398 --> 00:17:18.610
Thank you.

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:20.991
Okay, thank you.

00:17:21.051 --> 00:17:25.574
Yes, I understand.

00:17:25.634 --> 00:17:29.276
Hello, Anne.

00:17:29.336 --> 00:17:31.648
Or is it Ruth?

00:17:31.708 --> 00:17:34.169
You, again?

00:17:34.229 --> 00:17:35.269
Yes.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:39.262
And this time, you are coming with us.

00:17:39.322 --> 00:17:41.814
What are they doing?

00:17:41.874 --> 00:17:44.505
Her name's Ruth Street.

00:17:44.565 --> 00:17:47.206
They are taking her away.

00:17:47.266 --> 00:17:49.258
Are you Lily?

00:17:49.318 --> 00:17:52.338
Zoe Brewster's friend?

00:17:52.398 --> 00:17:56.460
Miss Brewster telephoned our office.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:18:00.842
Look at this from 2010.

00:18:00.902 --> 00:18:05.613
Ruth Street is doing it again.

00:18:05.673 --> 00:18:09.054
Stop Ruth Street.

00:18:09.114 --> 00:18:16.683
Police are hunting for street in an expensive hotel near a game reserve.

00:18:16.743 --> 00:18:22.554
She is buying rhino horn and taking it back to Europe.

00:18:22.615 --> 00:18:26.567
There, she is going to sell it on.

00:18:26.628 --> 00:18:29.320
Is there a problem?

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:31.342
That's Anne.

00:18:31.402 --> 00:18:34.594
It's a long story, Jeff.

00:18:34.654 --> 00:18:35.724
Yes.

00:18:35.784 --> 00:18:38.456
Let's go and have a drink.

00:18:38.516 --> 00:18:39.888
Excuse me.

00:18:39.908 --> 00:18:45.551
This is from the hotel for all of you.

00:18:45.611 --> 00:18:49.654
Breakfast with the big five.

00:18:49.714 --> 00:18:52.286
Five o'clock start.

00:18:52.346 --> 00:18:56.600
Groups of five or six people.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:58.762
Thank you.

00:18:58.822 --> 00:19:04.908
Tom, we're all going to see leopards tomorrow.

00:19:04.968 --> 00:19:06.450
And rhinos.

